From: lua-lsm-testsuite
Subject: [PATCH] run_qemu_anolis: add QEMU_MONITOR_SOCK env knob

Provide a Unix-socket QEMU monitor for clean guest shutdown via QMP. With a
monitor available, the harness can issue {"execute":"system_powerdown"} or
{"execute":"quit"} when a cell ends, which is faster and gentler than
SIGTERM->SIGKILL on the launcher PID.

Default empty preserves existing behaviour. When set, the path becomes a
Unix socket created by QEMU at startup with `,server,nowait` so the monitor
is reachable as soon as QEMU is up; the harness opens it on-demand.

This patch is shipped separately from the harness so it can be merged into
DebugKernel on its own schedule.

---
 run_qemu_anolis.sh | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/run_qemu_anolis.sh b/run_qemu_anolis.sh
--- a/run_qemu_anolis.sh
+++ b/run_qemu_anolis.sh
@@ -136,6 +136,8 @@ ROOT_DEV="${ROOT_DEV:-/dev/vda}"
 CONSOLE="${CONSOLE:-ttyS0}"
 KERNEL_CMDLINE="${KERNEL_CMDLINE:-}"
 EXTRA_CMDLINE="${EXTRA_CMDLINE:-}"
 QEMU_EXTRA_ARGS="${QEMU_EXTRA_ARGS:-}"
+QEMU_MONITOR_SOCK="${QEMU_MONITOR_SOCK:-}"

 ENABLE_GDB="${ENABLE_GDB:-0}"
 GDB_PORT="${GDB_PORT:-1235}"
@@ -274,6 +276,12 @@ if [[ "${DEBUG_WAIT}" == "1" ]]; then
     QEMU_ARGS+=(-S)
 fi

+if [[ -n "${QEMU_MONITOR_SOCK}" ]]; then
+    QEMU_ARGS+=(-monitor "unix:${QEMU_MONITOR_SOCK},server,nowait")
+fi
+
 if [[ -n "${QEMU_EXTRA_ARGS}" ]]; then
     read -r -a QEMU_EXTRA_ARGS_ARR <<< "${QEMU_EXTRA_ARGS}"
     QEMU_ARGS+=("${QEMU_EXTRA_ARGS_ARR[@]}")
--
